  "historical_output_text": " I still remember walking the same worn dirt road that ran from the old stone church down towards our village every morning before work during that particularly rough and storm-filled fall season when I turned 61; I was feeling more lost than ever in life. That's the way the weather felt outside, a heavy overpass cloud of storm fronts pressing on us from Canada and dragging their feet all the while. The rain that fell that fall had been a persistent and unwary visitor.\n\nOne crisp morning in November - I could see that from a small hole that now pock-marked and discolated in one of old Mother's hens' heads from an encounter a couple of winters prior; it still stood out stark in my peripheral - as usual I was trundelling down toward the village when suddenly the ground infront seemed a good foot lower.\n\nI",
